jobs.description:
A leading international pharmaceutical organisation in Berchem is looking for an Accountant to join their team. This full-time role offers the perfect mix of responsibility, variety, and professional growth within a supportive and international environment. With flexible working hours, attractive benefits, and a collaborative culture, this is your chance to make a real impact.

Your responsibilities as Accountant:

• A-Z responsibility of various VAT (BE + Other EU) declarations on monthly and quarterly basis;
• Assist the team in the daily operational accounting tasks (financial journals, purchase invoices,…);
• Back-up of other accountants;
• Cashflow-management (prepare foreign currency exchanges, ICO-payments, …)
• Preparing vendor payments in Isabel;
• Controlling and administrating the expense note application;
• Handling of the general finance mailbox
• Preparing and recording monthly accruals and deferrals;
• Assist in month-end and year-end closing;
• Assist in ad hoc projects to optimize current processes;
• The accounting team currently consists of 2 accountants.

Your profile as Accountant:

• Bachelor in Accountancy 
• First years of experience in similar roles
• Good knowledge of BE VAT
• Proficient in MS office
• Knowledge of MS AX and MS D365 is a plus
• Fluent in Dutch and English
• You are accurate and detail-oriented
• Proactive, stress-resistant, and eager to learn with strong analytical skills.

Our client is an international public affairs agency located in Brussels. 

Jobomschrijving

Do you have experience in working as an Office Manager in an international environment? Are you fluent in French and English? We have the right job for you! 

We are looking for an Office Manager (m/f/x) for one of our clients in Brussels. 

As Office Manager (m/f/x), you would be responsible for:

Perform administrative tasks for the office, e.g. relations with suppliers, organisation of office meetings and client visits;

Assist with onboarding of new staff;

Manage holiday plans and absences;

Contribute to website and social media channels;

Create content for clients’ websites and social media channels;

Handle invoices;

Liaise with external accountants to process invoices;

Produce expenditure reports;

Prepare content for client meetings, seminars and other events;

Other tasks: Ad-hoc support to client-related activities.

The successful candidate will be an experienced professional who demonstrates the following experiences and competencies:

Relevant degree

At least 2-3 years of working experience in similar positions

Full proficiency (writing and speaking) in English and French (an additional language is an asset);

Very good IT skills (e.g. command of MS Office, incl. in particular Excel, Powerpoint) Desirable

Strong organisational skills

Hard-working and flexible

Eye to detail; result-orientation

The role of this organisation is to represent the interests of its members on the EU political stage. Their main objective is to support the improvement of the commercial and regulatory environment for European rail operators and rail infrastructure companies.

Jobomschrijving

As part of your role you will : 

Managing a complex schedule of business meetings, conferences, personal appointments and travel.

Handling day-to-day correspondence and drafting business letters.

Preparing the form and content of all internal and external meetings and events for the Executive Director and taking minutes where necessary.

For internal and external meetings and events, you will research and collate documents and background information, prepare papers and presentations.

Organise statutory and high-level meetings.

Organise travel and bookings; manage all aspects of travel, logistics and expense claims.

If required, you will provide support at events.

Coordinating between the Executive Director and the team.

Minimum 8 years relevant work experience after obtaining a bachelor degree;

Fluency in written and spoken English and French, good knowledge of another major European language is considered a plus;

Excellent communication skills: verbal, written, repor writing and presentations;

Strong personal and excellent organisational skills;

A high degree of computer literacy - fully conversant with MS Office;

Strong time-management and multitasking abilities;

Positive mindset, professional attitude, solution oriented, and able to remain calm under pressure and keep to tight deadlines;

Team player, able to build good working relationships with colleagues;

A flexible and proactive attitude to work.
